# FILE: .cursor/rules/compute.mdc

---

description:
QUANTA deterministic compute rules
globs:

* app/compute/**
  alwaysApply: true

---

# ==================================================

# QUANTA COMPUTE ENGINE

# ==================================================

ROLE:

You are implementing deterministic statistical computation.

You NEVER interpret.

You NEVER explain.

You NEVER generate conclusions.

You only compute.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
COMPUTE PRINCIPLES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Compute must be:

deterministic
pure
reproducible
traceable

# Same input

same output

No randomness unless explicit.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
INPUT RULES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

All inputs validated.

Reject:

* empty dataset
* duplicated columns
* unsupported dtype
* corrupted rows

Normalize:

* NaN
* inf
* categories
* encoding

Never mutate original dataframe.

Always:

df_clean = df.copy()

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
STATISTICAL SAFETY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Before every test:

validate assumptions.

Examples:

t-test:

* normality
* independence
* variance

anova:

* homogeneity

correlation:

* distribution
* outliers

If assumptions fail:

DO NOT CONTINUE.

Return:

alternative_test
reason

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
LIKERT RULES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Likert handling:

1–5
1–7

Treat as ordinal.

Forbidden:

automatic mean comparison.

Allowed:

Mann Whitney

Kruskal

Dunn
(scikit-posthocs)

Ordinal regression.

If treated continuous:

must justify.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
MISSING VALUES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Never silently remove.

Missing strategy:

<5%
warn

5–20%
explicit strategy

> 20%
> low confidence

Log:

reason
method

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
NUMERICAL SAFETY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Every compute function:

protect against:

NaN

inf

overflow

underflow

empty arrays

constant vectors

division by zero

insufficient n

Always:

raise domain exception.

Never:

return None

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
COMMENTS RULE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Never remove:

* formulas
* derivations
* mathematical notes

Preserve research intent.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
OUTPUT RULE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Outputs:

strict models.

Never raw dict.

Include:

inputs

method

statistics

assumptions

warnings

audit

confidence

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
DOCUMENTATION
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Prefer:

@Docs Pandas

@Docs Scipy

@Docs Statsmodels

@Docs scikit-posthocs
